# Little Browser: the phone shell's hooks (chromium/lb/android, app.littlebrowser.lb.shell;
# docs/android-ui.md, docs/ux.md §10). The tabbed activity's UI coordinator makes the shell on its
# tab model, sheets and tab thumbnails. Every way into Chromium's tab switcher (the Hub: the tab
# count, swiping the bar up, the last tab closing) shows the all-tabs view instead. The home
# button is the space button, which opens the spaces sheet. A user closing one pinned tab puts it
# to sleep (docs/ux.md §6). The ⋯ menu gets the shell's own items, Pin and Move to Space. On
# tablets the shell doesn't run and Chromium's own behaviour stays.

